    "body": "Vite+ exposes `vp` but no longer provides a standalone `oxlint` binary. The oxlint config already recognizes Vite+ projects, but it only looks for `oxlint`, so the language server fails to start when a project uses Vite+ without a separate oxlint installation.\n\nLook for `oxlint` and `vp` in the project's `node_modules/.bin` before checking `PATH`. Keep `oxlint` preferred within each location, and start `vp` with `lint --lsp` when selected.\n\nRelated discussion: https://github.com/voidzero-dev/vite-plus/pull/3016. That PR proposed restoring the editor binaries; the discussion explains that the wrappers were removed because they could conflict with the upstream packages during installation.\n\nValidation: 48 executable-discovery cases in headless Neovim using temporary executable files, StyLua, LuaLS diagnostics, and the repository lint script all pass.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-13T15:17:45Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
